{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "U1: Use Apache Curator's built-in namespace support (chroot suffix on the ZooKeeper connection string, e.g. host:port/tenant-x) so that all existing ZK paths are automatically isolated per tenant without rewriting path logic; expose the namespace as a configurable property in servers.yml / xd-admin connection settings.",
    "U2: Implement interactive credential entry in xd-shell using the JLine console reader with password masking (echo disabled); credentials are held only in memory and sent to the Admin server via HTTP Basic Auth headers over the existing REST client; no credentials are written to disk, logs, or command history.",
    "U3: Adopt a Gitflow-style maintenance branch (e.g., 1.0.x) cut from the 1.0.1 release tag; configure a dedicated CI build plan for the branch and document the cherry-pick/merge-back policy; MASTER continues as the minor/feature line.",
    "U4: Remove deprecated module-registry functions (including download of module definitions) and dead code in Shell and Admin-UI modules; rely on compiler deprecation warnings, static analysis, and full regression suite to verify no behavioral change.",
    "U5: Publish the Admin server's actual bound host/port (including the Tomcat-generated random port) as an ephemeral ZooKeeper node at startup; xd-shell discovers the endpoint by reading that node ('admin connect' command). A load balancer is explicitly deferred per spike outcome; direct ZK-based discovery is chosen as the interim mechanism.",
    "U6: Upgrade the Kafka client dependency to the 0.9 new consumer API (KafkaConsumer) and refactor the Kafka message bus to the new API, then rerun and fix the known failing integration tests against an embedded/broker test fixture.",
    "U7: Implement ingest as a new Motion-JPEG (MJPEG over HTTP multipart/x-mixed-replace) stream source module that emits frame messages (byte arrays with content-type image/jpeg plus metadata) for downstream analytics processors. Pure-Java frame parsing is used; native OpenCV bindings are excluded because they are not platform-compatible. Actual facial-detection algorithm implementation is out of scope (spike + ingest + design spec only).",
    "U8: Add a boolean property (e.g., xd.ui.messageRates.enabled) in servers.yml, surfaced through the Admin server's /management/config REST endpoint; the Admin-UI cluster view conditionally renders message-rate columns based on the flag, defaulting to enabled."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The existing Spring XD-style codebase (xd-shell, Admin server, module registry, Kafka message bus, Admin-UI) builds cleanly and the development environment (JDK, build tools, ZooKeeper/Kafka test fixtures) is already provisioned; environment setup effort is excluded.",
    "All work is performed by a single developer (the author); estimates are effort (work-hours), not elapsed time, and include unit/integration test work within each activity.",
    "For U3, the effort covers branch creation, CI plan configuration, versioning scheme, and a short branching-policy document; ongoing release management on the branch is excluded.",
    "For U5, no load balancer is provisioned in this increment; delivering the LB option is out of scope after the spike concludes ZK-based discovery is acceptable for experimentation.",
    "For U6, the set of failing tests is already identified; upgrading transitive dependencies (e.g., matching broker versions in the test harness) is included in the activity estimate.",
    "For U7, audio ingest is delivered as a secondary input mode of the same stream source (PCM/WAV payload support); the predictive-analytics (facial detection) implementation itself is out of scope, limited to feasibility research and a written design specification.",
    "For U8, the Admin-UI is the existing web UI of the product and already consumes a config endpoint, so only additive changes are needed.",
    "Code review, rework, and merge effort is embedded in each activity estimate; no separate contingency is added.",
    "Documentation effort covers updates to reference docs and release notes only; no full documentation rewrite is required."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Configurable ZooKeeper namespace per tenant",
      "activity_description": "Add a tenant-scoped ZK namespace/chroot configuration property, wire it into Curator client creation for admin, containers, and shell, verify all metadata paths are isolated, and add integration tests with two namespaces sharing one ensemble.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Interactive Admin server login in xd-shell",
      "activity_description": "Implement interactive username/password prompting (masked input) in xd-shell, in-memory credential handling, Basic Auth propagation to Admin REST calls, and unit/integration tests including auth failure and non-interactive fallback.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U3 - Maintenance branch setup",
      "activity_description": "Create the 1.0.x maintenance branch from the release tag, adjust version numbers, configure the branch CI build plan, and document the branching/cherry-pick policy for MINOR releases.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Cleanup of deprecated module registry code",
      "activity_description": "Remove deprecated module-registry functions (including module definition download), clean up residual deprecated code in Shell and Admin-UI modules, fix all call sites, and run the full regression suite to confirm no behavioral change.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Spike: admin endpoint discovery approach",
      "activity_description": "Research and compare direct xd-shell-to-ZooKeeper discovery versus load-balancer-mediated discovery, including Hadoop/HDFS client ZK-access constraints; produce a short decision record recommending the interim approach.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Admin port publication and shell discovery",
      "activity_description": "Publish the Admin server's actual bound host/port (random Tomcat port) as an ephemeral ZK node at startup; implement xd-shell discovery and an 'admin connect' command that targets the discovered endpoint; add integration tests with random-port admin instances.",
      "most_likely_effort": 28
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Kafka new consumer API upgrade and test stabilization",
      "activity_description": "Upgrade the Kafka client to the 0.9 rewritten consumer, refactor the Kafka message bus (subscription, offset management, error handling) to the new API, and rerun and fix the previously failing integration tests until green.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Spike: Motion-JPEG feasibility and design spec",
      "activity_description": "Research Motion-JPEG feasibility for streaming ingest, assess the platform-compatibility constraints of OpenCV, evaluate pure-Java frame parsing options, and write the design specification for the A/V ingest module and downstream analytics integration.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Audio/video (Motion-JPEG) ingest source module",
      "activity_description": "Implement an MJPEG-over-HTTP stream source module that parses multipart frames and emits frame messages with metadata, plus PCM/WAV audio input support; provide a sample processor wiring for downstream facial-detection analytics; add unit and integration tests with recorded streams.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "U8 - servers.yml toggle for message rates in cluster view",
      "activity_description": "Add the enable/disable config parameter in servers.yml, expose it via the Admin server's config REST endpoint, and update the Admin-UI cluster view to conditionally render message-rate columns; add tests for both settings.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Cross-increment integration and system testing",
      "activity_description": "Perform end-to-end system testing across all delivered stories (multi-tenant ZK isolation with secured shell access, Kafka bus regression, A/V ingest pipeline, UI toggle), including defect fixing uncovered during system test.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "Documentation and release notes",
      "activity_description": "Update reference documentation (new properties, shell commands, ingest module, branching policy) and write release notes covering all stories in the increment.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 272
  }
}
